    "helpful_mechanics": "Automatic transmission removes shift management; automatic recovery returns the car to the track after crashes; top-down camera shows the road layout far ahead; combined throttle+steer inputs allow smooth cornering; stage scoring awards points from segment coverage even without a finish, and finishing itself is worth 4 points per stage.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "One-second action granularity with a fast car causes steering overshoot and late reactions; the car can rotate and slide, so corrections must be anticipated; wall-clock thinking time is charged against the 3-hour budget; a single failed stage blocks all subsequent stage scoring; slow corners and drift physics punish coarse control."
